[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71245,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myopericytoma is a perivascular myoid neoplasm, which rarely affects the genitourinary tract.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71246,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8824/0 Myopericytoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71247,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F34 &amp; XH2HE9 Benign neoplasm of male genital organs &amp; Myopericytoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71248,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> myofibroma of the glans penis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71249,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71250,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myopericytomas typically occur within the dermis or subcutis of distal extremities; visceral involvement is rare. They rarely affect the genitourinary tract, but they have been reported in the kidney and bladder {26191123; 24746217}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71251,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal myopericytomas are usually asymptomatic and disclosed incidentally during examination for other reasons {26191123}. Patients with bladder tumours presented with gross haematuria or dysuria and urinary frequency {24746217; 28214470}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71252,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal myopericytomas are observed exclusively in adults, with a male predominance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71253,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myopericytomas may occur on a familial basis, but no such association has been noted in genitourinary cases {24746217; 26191123}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71254,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Abnormalities/mutations of the <em>PDGFRB</em> gene are common in myopericytomas but are not specific to these entities {27776010; 28505006}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71255,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal myopericytoma is usually a well-circumscribed, solid, rubbery tumour with a variable colour (grey-tan to red-brown). The size of renal and other genitourinary cases ranges from 18&nbsp;to 73&nbsp;mm {28214470; 24746217; 26191123}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71256,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myopericytoma is characterized by a perivascular concentric proliferation of bland, oval to spindle-shaped cells. Nuclei are usually round to spindled, and they may rarely show degenerative features. Numerous thin-walled vessels are always present. Stroma is oedematous and can exhibit hyalinization or myxoid change. Necrosis may be present {24746217}. Some cases show more pronounced whorled or fascicular architecture, similar to that seen in myofibromas {16394283}.</p>\r\n<p>By immunohistochemistry, myopericytomas express SMA and h-caldesmon, whereas only focal positivity is observed with desmin and/or CD34 {24746217; 26191123}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71257,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71258,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71259,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> bland, myoid-like cells growing in a concentric perivascular pattern.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> SMA positivity, <em>PDGFRB</em> alterations.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71260,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71261,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 329,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myopericytomas are benign lesions and complete surgical resection is curative. They do not recur or metastasize. Exceedingly rare malignant myopericytomas have been described outside the genitourinary tract, which had a poor outcome {12405913}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T14:53:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]